PicoML compilation to WebAssembly no longer works after the refactor

Our PicoML tooling used to parse expressions, infer their types, and compile them to WebAssembly, including comparisons on integers, booleans, floats, and lists. We need that flow working again so programs can run through the compiler's JavaScript bindings.

```ts
import { parse, compile, generateBinary, toBoolean } from "pico-ml";
const ast = parse("let threshold = 7 in threshold < 12").unwrap();
const mod = compile(ast).unwrap();
const binary = generateBinary(mod, { enableNameSection: false }).unwrap();
const { instance } = await WebAssembly.instantiate(binary, {});
const result = toBoolean(instance, (instance.exports.main as () => number)());
```

This should produce an executable module and decode its result as a JavaScript boolean. Instead, the remaining stubs throw `"not implemented"`.

Restore the affected implementation in `pico-ml` (`packages/core`). Under `src/`, the throwing stubs are in `compiler/` (including `compiler.ts`, `assets/modules/comparator.ts`, and `js-bindings.ts`), `syntax/parser.ts`, `syntax/tokenizer.ts`, `type-checker/`, `structure/result.ts`, `wasm/wat/ast-factory.ts`, `wasm/wat/tokenizer.ts`, and `wasm/converter/convert-node/elem.ts`, `table.ts`, and `typedef.ts`. This includes the supporting runtime modules, expression compilation, type inference, and WebAssembly utilities needed by that flow, with the existing compilation options working again. Runtime module entry points mus
